Upgrade procedure for tnftp (ftp(1))

Source:		https://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/misc/tnftp/tnftp-VERSION.tar.gz
Signature:	https://ftp.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/misc/tnftp/tnftp-VERSION.tar.gz.asc
Signing key:	Luke Mewburn <lukem@NetBSD.org>
		DSA 1024, 2A8E 22ED B07B 5414 548D  8507 A418 6D9A 7F33 2472
		(also listed in Debian's debian/upstream/signing-key.asc
		and Arch Linux's tnftp PKGBUILD validpgpkeys; pkgsrc
		net/tnftp/distinfo carries the SHA512 of each release)

Vendor branch:	vendor/NetBSD/tnftp	(tags vendor/NetBSD/tnftp/VERSION)
In-tree prefix:	contrib/tnftp
Build glue:	usr.bin/ftp (Makefile, tnftp_config.h)

The vendor branch holds the complete, unmodified release tarball at its
root, including the exec bits of the files upstream ships executable.
Nothing is pruned, so there is no MIDNIGHTBSD-Xlist.  (Before 20260211
the branch used an svn-style layout with dist/, 20141031/ and 20100108/
directories; the 20260211 import replaced that with the plain tarball.)

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download the tarball and its .asc into an empty directory and verify
   the signature with the key above.  Compare the SHA512 with pkgsrc.
2. Use the vendor-update skill: stage the extracted tarball with
   "git add -A -f" (temporary index or worktree), check that the staged
   tree matches the tarball including exec bits, and commit it on
   vendor/NetBSD/tnftp as "Vendor import of tnftp VERSION".
3. Merge the vendor commit into contrib/tnftp on master and the stable
   branches as a real merge ("Merge commit '<sha>'"), never squashed.
4. Update usr.bin/ftp/tnftp_config.h (see below) and usr.bin/ftp/Makefile
   if upstream's src/Makefile.am source list changed.

tnftp_config.h:

  usr.bin/ftp/tnftp_config.h is maintained by hand; configure is not run.
  For each new release, diff the old and new tnftp_config.h.in and carry
  the changes over: bump PACKAGE_STRING, PACKAGE_VERSION and VERSION,
  remove entries that are gone, and define each new HAVE_* only after
  checking that our headers and libc provide it.  Then check that every
  HAVE_*, USE_* and WITH_* macro referenced by tnftp.h and the src/ files
  that are built is either defined or really absent on MidnightBSD.

  Notes on the current settings:
  - HAVE_LOCALE_H must stay defined.  src/main.c and src/util.c get
    <locale.h> only through tnftp.h.  It was lost when tnftp_config.h
    was replaced with FreeBSD's 20100108 copy in 2022, and setlocale()
    was then disabled with "#if 0" in main.c and util.c to get the build
    going again; 20260211 dropped those changes and restored the define.
  - USE_INET6 is left undefined; the Makefile adds -DINET6 unless
    WITHOUT_INET6_SUPPORT is set.
  - USE_GLOB_H is defined: our <glob.h> has GLOB_BRACE, GLOB_NOCHECK and
    GLOB_TILDE, which is what configure tests for.
  - The AC_USE_SYSTEM_EXTENSIONS macros (_GNU_SOURCE, _ALL_SOURCE, ...)
    and _POSIX_SOURCE/_POSIX_1_SOURCE/_MINIX are left undefined so that
    the default BSD namespace is used.
  - WITH_SSL is left undefined (see below).

SSL / https:

  ftp(1) is built without WITH_SSL and is not linked against libssl or
  libcrypto, so https:// URLs are not supported; fetch(1) handles them.
  Unlike 20141031, src/ssl.c in 20260211 also holds the plain fetch_*()
  connection I/O used by src/fetch.c for every http:// transfer, so
  ssl.c is in SRCS but compiled without WITH_SSL: all OpenSSL code in
  it is behind "#ifdef WITH_SSL".  Check after each update that the
  binary has no SSL_* references (nm) and no libssl/libcrypto (ldd).

Libraries:

  ftp(1) uses the base system libedit (LIBADD=edit).  The bundled
  contrib/tnftp/libedit and contrib/tnftp/libnetbsd are not built.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  None as of 20260211.  contrib/tnftp is identical to the vendor tree
  apart from this file.

  Patches dropped in the 20260211 update:
  - src/ftp.c abort_remote(): "unsigned char buf[BUFSIZ]" (local commit
    43de880bd2) is upstream now.
  - tnftp.h: unconditional "#include <sys/uio.h>" (local commit
    c1aa790823); upstream now includes it under HAVE_SYS_UIO_H.
  - src/main.c, src/util.c: "#if 0" around setlocale() (local commits
    81454a505b and b89d4b69c5), see HAVE_LOCALE_H above.

  FreeBSD patches that were never carried here and are not needed:
  - FreeBSD 43092b7d087d (SO_SNDBUF/SO_RCVBUF breaking TCP buffer
    autosizing): since 20260211 the socket buffer sizes default to 0
    ("autoscale") and tnftp only calls setsockopt() for them once a size
    is set (-x, the sndbuf/rcvbuf commands, or internally after a
    file:// URL), so autosizing is kept by default.
  - FreeBSD 47cc9ee1b1d4 (default pager "less"): we keep upstream's
    "more".
